      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The injection of retrobulbar block is associated with significant pain and discomfort. Therefore a short-acting IV analgesic before retrobulbar injection has been advocated."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To compare remifentanil, alfentanil and fentanyl in providing analgesia for retrobulbar block injection."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "69 patients were enrolled randomly into three groups of 23 each to receive either Remifentanil 1 microg/kg, Alfentanil 20 microg/kg or Fentanyl 2 microg/kg as an IV bolus dose prior to retrobulbar injection. Mean arterial pressure (MAP) and heart rate (HR) were recorded and Numerical Pain Score (NPS) were assessed by a blinded observer."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Remifentanil prevented increase in MAP and HR while alfentanil and fentanyl were ineffective in this purpose (p < 0.05). NPS was significantly lower in remifentanil group (p < 0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Remifentanil 1 microg/kg prior to retrobulbar injection provide excellent hemodynamic stability and ensure analgesia."
        }
      ]},
